Package: gideon
Version: @VERSION@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Ankit Chhetri <achhetri@webmd.net>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3-gi (>= 3.48), python3-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
 libgtk-3-0t64, libglib2.0-0t64, libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0,
 libasound2t64, libstdc++6, libgcc-s1, procps,
 dbus-user-session, systemd
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Suggests: ollama
Description: Fully local, offline voice assistant for Ubuntu
 Gideon listens for a wake word, transcribes what you say, answers with a
 local language model and speaks the reply back - entirely on-device, with
 no cloud APIs. A tray icon also lets you type a question directly.
 .
 The package bundles its own Python runtime, openWakeWord, faster-whisper,
 Piper TTS, PortAudio and every model weight it needs, so installing it
 requires no network access at all.
 .
 The language-model step talks to a local Ollama instance, which is the one
 component not bundled here. See /usr/share/doc/gideon/README.Debian.
